WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.089
In 2014, Russian President Vladimir Putin
was not very popular among Republicans or

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.089
Democrats.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:09.249
Which made sense given that he's a somewhat murderous

00:00:09.249 --> 00:00:12.600
strongman with the nasty habit of invading his neighbors.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.570
This is, without question, our number one geopolitical foe.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.420
Breaking news, signs of a Russian invasion
in Ukraine tonight.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:22.590
Since 2000, 25 journalists have died under
mysterious circumstances.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.060
The Russian military campaign in Syria after
a week of airstrikes now escalating dramatically

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.380
to prop up Syrian president Assad.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.000
This chart
shows Putin’s net favorability among Republicans.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.440
That's the percentage of people who view him favorably

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.500
minus the
percent who view him unfavorably.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.100
You can see the net favorability
begin to rise steadily through 2014 and 2015,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.329
and then, all of a sudden, in August 2016,
it spikes.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:01:00.190
By December 2016, the share of Republicans
who saw Putin favorably had more than tripled.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:06.860
His popularity fell among Democrats, but by a smaller margin. So, what’s going on here?

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.760
And what does it mean for the United States’
relationship with Russia?

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.180
What I think you're seeing is two years of constant Republican

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.240
propaganda about how Vladimir Putin is a strong leader.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.220
Putin decides what he wants to do and he does
it in half a day...He makes a decision and

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:26.809
he executes it, quickly, then everybody reacts.

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:31.840
That’s what you call a leader. People are
looking at Putin as one who wrestles bears

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.040
and drills for oil.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.590
They look at our president as one who wears
mom jeans.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:41.450
What you see is this Republican talking point
that builds and builds and builds, and finally

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.780
really hits a peak with Donald Trump.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.549
I think I’d get along very well with him.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.780
I respect Putin.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:46.800
He’s a strong leader.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.680
If he says great things about me I’m going
to say great things about him.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.450
I’ve already said, he is very much of a
leader.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.979
I mean you can say, “Oh isn’t that a terrible
thing.”

00:01:54.979 --> 00:01:57.900
The man has very strong control over a country.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.509
What we're seeing with Donald Trump is that
he believes in the "Great Man Theory" of history,

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.119
both the great part of it and also the man
part of it.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:08.479
He's a man who sees himself as a tough decisive
leader, authoritarian if necessary but willing

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:10.970
to do whatever it takes to push through what
he thinks needs to be done.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:15.090
He looks to Vladimir Putin in Russia, someone
who has made clear, if you're a dissident

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.950
who criticizes him you may disappear, if you're
someone in the public who isn't fully in support

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.180
of him, you may lose your job.

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:22.529
And he looks at that and thinks, it works.

00:02:22.529 --> 00:02:24.529
There's also a financial connection.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.480
Trump has had trouble getting
loans from US banks following his multiple

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.439
bankruptcy filings since 1991.

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:36.469
We know from a speech his son, Donald Jr.,
made in 2008 that Russian investors have played

00:02:36.469 --> 00:02:41.040
a big role in financing Trump projects since.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.909
Most wealthy Russian business people maintain
warm relationships with Putin, who holds absolute

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:47.680
power in the country.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.109
That means the investors who helped save Trump’s
business empire are likely to include several

00:02:52.109 --> 00:02:53.149
close Putin allies.

00:02:53.149 --> 00:02:56.500
We're in this extraordinary moment when a US President

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.340
is potentially financially beholden to an enemy country led by a dictator.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.000
There's an intelligence report
in which a former British spy claims the Russian

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.439
government has compromising information on
Trump that they could use to blackmail him.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.519
This isn't Hollywood, this isn't conspiracy,
this isn't paranoia, this may actually on

00:03:14.519 --> 00:03:15.889
some level be true.

00:03:15.889 --> 00:03:21.159
Republican voters may be taking their cues from Trump when it comes to Putin, but Republican lawmakers

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.159
are a different story.

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:24.339
Vladimir Putin is a person who's killed.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.440
He's jailed and murdered journalists, political opponents.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.860
Putin is an aggressor that does not share
our interests.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:35.589
Vladimir Putin is violating the sovereignty
of neighboring countries.

00:03:35.589 --> 00:03:40.609
It certainly appears he is conducting in state-sponsored
cyber attacks on what appears to be

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.800
our political system.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.640
The Russians undermining democracy throughout the entire world.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.520
They're taking land owned by others by force.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.740
They did hack into our political system, they're doing it to other political systems.

00:03:52.749 --> 00:03:57.100
Before he was Donald Trump’s Vice President, then-Representative Mike Pence held

00:03:57.109 --> 00:03:58.109
a similar position.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.579
And now an increasingly antagonistic
Russia has been rewarded for bullying and

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:06.650
threatening its neighbors.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.950
Seven years later, he was singing a different
tune.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:15.849
I think it’s inarguable that Vladimir Putin
has been a stronger leader in his country

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:19.200
than Barack Obama has been in this country.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:25.160
When Trump praises Putin, he’s also flouting
his party’s long history of skepticism toward Russia.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.960
When you think of Republicans and the kind
of leader they venerate, it's Ronald Reagan.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.040
They come back to Reagan again and again and
again.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.690
I remember when Ronald Reagan was the president.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.030
He stood on principle standing up to the Soviet
Union.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:43.680
Ronald Reagan reignited the American economy,
rebuilt the military, bankrupted the Soviet

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.580
Union and defeated Soviet communism.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.230
And they come back to him because they think
he won the Cold War, and because they think

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.660
he beat the Soviet Union.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.400
The march of freedom and democracy which will
leave Marxism-Leninism on the ash heap of

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.950
history as it has left other tyrannies which
stifle the freedom and muzzle the self-expression

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.400
of the people.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.510
This is not just a break from Republicans
on the Hill in 2016, this is a break with

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:10.320
the last 30 years of ideology, dating back to a President,

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.320
Ronald Reagan, who they hold up as a near god-like figure.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.180
Trump has also been slow to accept the CIA
and FBI’s conclusion that Russia sought

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.170
to influence the Presidential election.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.610
Russia hacked the Democratic National Committee Servers,

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.050
it hacked the personal email of John Podesta, Hillary Clinton's campaign chairman

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:34.020
As far as hacking I think it was Russia, but I think we also get hacked by other countries and other people.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.080
Vladimir Putin weaponized the fact that we
have a free press.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:42.520
He used Wikileaks to kind of launder the information,
and then dribbled it out day by day by day.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.520
So for weeks, in the run up to the election,
all you saw was negative press coverage of

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.140
Hillary Clinton driven by selectively chosen
leaked emails.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.220
In response, President Obama issued economic
sanctions against Russia,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.480
which Donald Trump doesn't have to keep

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.380
These were weak, these sanctions, they're
gonna do nothing.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:03.220
Vladimir Putin will look at this and
say, I got what I wanted, I can pay this cost,

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:03.920
I'll do it again.

